From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua Warren <816217+joshuaswarren@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 02:32:58 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: apple: pmp-report: hold the AGX request 250 ms
 after the last operation

A 9B model at 8192 tokens of context had one gap of up to 111.5 ms between
two decoded tokens in every process, once per run, with the GPU idle for a
good part of it. The 100 ms default hold dropped the request in that gap,
which costs one slow token while the PMP raises memory again. The longest
gap in any other configuration measured was 64 ms.

Raise the default to 250 ms, about 2.2 times the longest gap seen. The cost
is a few hundred milliseconds of the higher memory state after the last
job. pmp_report.agx_vote_idle_ms still overrides it at run time.

The default is one constant, AGX_VOTE_IDLE_MS_DEFAULT, used for both the
parameter and the initial state. The userspace test has a case that rides
through a 112 ms gap with the default and still drops the request after a
long idle.

Signed-off-by: Joshua Warren <816217+joshuaswarren@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit 5b54de318780297d6a4ebdc11e24bc39f4132029)
---
 drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-agx-vote.h | 4 ++++
 drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c   | 6 +++---
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-agx-vote.h b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-agx-vote.h
index 70ad71c514..715ab63e42 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-agx-vote.h
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-agx-vote.h
@@ -22,6 +22,10 @@ typedef uint32_t agx_ms_t;
 typedef int32_t agx_sms_t;
 #endif
 
+/* How long the request is held after the last operation ends. w7X measured idle gaps of up to 111.5 ms inside one 9B generation, so 100 ms
+ * was not enough; 250 ms is about 2.2 times the largest gap seen. The parameter pmp_report.agx_vote_idle_ms overrides it at run time. */
+#define AGX_VOTE_IDLE_MS_DEFAULT 250
+
 /* After a set that was not acknowledged (or a PMP that is not running), wait this long before trying again. */
 #define AGX_VOTE_RETRY_MS 1000
 
diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
index d5823dd3d2..ef01d9a21a 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
@@ -86,7 +86,7 @@ static const struct apple_pmp_report_offsets apple_pmp_offsets_t600x;
 /* T6001 AGX request (see the engine below set_state): AGX is soc-device record 9 on the T6001. */
 #define APPLE_PMP_T6001_AGX_ID 9
 static bool agx_vote;
-static struct agx_vote apple_pmp_agx_vote_state = {.idle_ms = 100};
+static struct agx_vote apple_pmp_agx_vote_state = {.idle_ms = AGX_VOTE_IDLE_MS_DEFAULT};
 static DEFINE_SPINLOCK(apple_pmp_agx_vote_lock);
 /* Serializes the vote work, the unbind release and the report's removal. */
 static DEFINE_MUTEX(apple_pmp_agx_vote_mutex);
@@ -1339,7 +1339,7 @@ static int apple_pmp_report_set_state(struct apple_pmp_report *rep, u32 id,
  * GPU unbind and when this report goes away. The decisions are in pmp-agx-vote.h (unit tested); this is the glue.
  * Off by default (pmp_report.agx_vote): with it off nothing is written.
  */
-static unsigned int agx_vote_idle_ms = 100;
+static unsigned int agx_vote_idle_ms = AGX_VOTE_IDLE_MS_DEFAULT;
 
 static agx_ms_t apple_pmp_agx_now_ms(void)
 {
@@ -1367,7 +1367,7 @@ static const struct kernel_param_ops apple_pmp_agx_vote_ops = {
 module_param_cb(agx_vote, &apple_pmp_agx_vote_ops, &agx_vote, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(agx_vote, "T6001: set the AGX power request in the PMP report while the GPU has work in flight (default: off)");
 module_param(agx_vote_idle_ms, uint, 0644);
-MODULE_PARM_DESC(agx_vote_idle_ms, "Keep the AGX request this many ms after the last GPU operation ends (default: 100)");
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(agx_vote_idle_ms, "Keep the AGX request this many ms after the last GPU operation ends (default: 250)");
 
 /* Write the AGX request of the bound T6001 report: -ENODEV without one, -EAGAIN (nothing written) when the PMP does not run. */
 static int apple_pmp_agx_write(bool enable, bool no_ack)
